#### Principle 2: Module Scope = Store Scope

**Description:** In a micro-frontend architecture, each module's Zustand store must be scoped to that module and cleaned up when the module unmounts. A Zustand store must never be shared across a Module Federation boundary.

**Rationale:** Sharing a store across a Module Federation boundary creates the same coupling problem as sharing a Redux store — it breaks module independence and creates version entanglement. Each module is a vertical slice that owns its own state lifecycle.

**Application:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Module-scoped store, cleaned up on unmount
// claims-mfe/src/store/claimsStore.ts
import { create } from 'zustand';

interface ClaimsUIState {
  selectedClaimId: string | null;
  filterStatus: 'all' | 'pending' | 'approved' | 'denied';
  isDetailPanelOpen: boolean;
}

export const useClaimsStore = create<ClaimsUIState>(() => ({
  selectedClaimId: null,
  filterStatus: 'all',
  isDetailPanelOpen: false,
}));

// claims-mfe/src/App.tsx - Cleanup on unmount
export default function ClaimsApp() {
  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      // Clear module state on unmount
      useClaimsStore.setState({
        selectedClaimId: null,
        filterStatus: 'all',
        isDetailPanelOpen: false,
      });
    };
  }, []);

  return <ClaimsRoutes />;
}
```

