#### Best Practice 2: One Store Per Domain Concern

**Description:** Create small, focused Zustand stores per domain concern within a module rather than a single monolithic store.

**Rationale:** Multiple small stores prevent unnecessary re-renders — components subscribe only to the slice they need. It mirrors the micro-frontend domain decomposition principle (one module per business capability) at the state level.

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Separate stores per concern
export const useSearchStore = create<SearchState>(...);       // Search filters, pagination
export const useSelectionStore = create<SelectionState>(...); // Selected items, detail panel
export const useWorkflowStore = create<WorkflowState>(...);   // Wizard step, validation state

// Components subscribe only to what they need
function SearchBar() {
  const { query, setQuery } = useSearchStore(); // Only re-renders on search changes
}

function DetailPanel() {
  const { selectedId } = useSelectionStore(); // Only re-renders on selection changes
}

// ❌ WRONG: Monolithic store (mirrors Redux anti-pattern)
export const useClaimsStore = create<{
  searchQuery: string;
  selectedId: string | null;
  wizardStep: number;
  // ...20 more fields
}>(...);
```

**Success Indicators:** No component subscribes to more state fields than it visually renders; re-render profiling shows components updating only when their specific subscribed state changes.

